let __v_256 = Value::from("The own-brand box is the same medicine for less: match the active ingredient and the dose on the back, and a pharmacy's own hay fever or painkiller tablet is usually a fraction of the branded price. Ask the pharmacist to put the two boxes side by side if the names confuse - the licence number and the ingredient are the parts that must match, not the box. The one place it matters is a medicine you take for something serious, where the brand can change how much you absorb.");
frame.store("_OWN_BRAND_CARD", __v_256.clone())?;
let __v_257 = Value::from("It cannot be bought over the counter - a prescription-only medicine is not sold off the shelf whatever the box looks like - but ordering more is a different question, and most pharmacies will send the repeat request to the surgery for you and have it ready in two or three days. Ask at the counter, and order about a week before you run out. If the course did not work, say so when you order: the same thing again is often not what the doctor would choose.");
frame.store("_PRESCRIBED_CARD", __v_257.clone())?;
let __v_258 = Value::from("Nothing from the chemist - a pharmacy's shelves are dosed for people, and a dog or cat can be poisoned by what is ordinary for us (paracetamol and ibuprofen especially, and some decongestants). Ring the vet for anything that lasts more than a day or two, and keep every medicine you buy out of reach, child locks and all. The one thing a pharmacy can do is tell you what is poisonous, so keep the box to read out.");
